      "id": "sol.ahsme-1983-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Taking \\(u=x-y\\) and \\(v=y,\\) the sine addition identity gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\sin(x-y)\\cos y\\\\ &\\quad+\\cos(x-y)\\sin y\\\\ &=\\sin((x-y)+y)=\\sin x. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Recognize the sine addition identity",
        "Apply the sine addition formula with \\(u=x-y\\) and \\(v=y\\)"
